{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01JrcgGmf6xMAgjgaPmrFUEH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D25 seen, D26+ forecast)\n2\t\n3\tScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\n4\tGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 25 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\n5\tTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\n6\tin `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native/indexed/\n7\treflection) on D1-D19. D15\n8\tadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\n9\tMastery. D16 (JNI Boundary) TT/Mastery builds added the first REAL gate in code: `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int\n10\tlen)` returns `arena_value` only if `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -- still with the literal in the asset and `.rodata`.\n11\tD17 (Name Collapse, R8-style identifier collapse) left the native track: 6-entry fixture, new per-char permutation codec\n12\t`indexed`, one renamed class `a`; the TT dex carried the real hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy` strings.\n13\tD18 (Encrypted Strings, `string_decryption` \"runtime string decryption\"): 6-entry fixture, codec `xor` again (b64 + 1-byte\n14\tkey); single dex had no cipher code, the TT/Mastery dex added class `EncryptedStrings` method `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n15\tD19 (Reflection Maze, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\n16\tgenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\n17\tclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\n18\tD20 (Loaded Later, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\"; prompt \"Analyze a challenge-signed secondary DEX and recover\n19\tthe module contract\"): 7-entry APK with `assets/payload.dex` (508 B, plain dex 035); NEW codec `dynamic` whose `data` is\n20\tthe ENTRY PATH `assets/payload.dex` -- the FIRST day the answer left the JSON value: a plain `ANS-` const in payload class\n21\t`com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:..`). No ClassLoader/verify code\n22\tin any host dex; TT/Mastery host dex added `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`.\n23\tD21 (Debug Me If You Can, `anti_debug` \"anti-debug state checks\"; prompt \"Neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine\n24\twhile retaining the intended app flow\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse` (d2/d8) -- the D20 pointer did\n25\tNOT persist. First manifest with `android:debuggable=\"true\"` (single/TT/Mastery-d21 only). No debugger/TracerPid/clock\n26\tAPI and no state loop in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n27\tD22 (Root of Trust, `root_detection` \"synthetic root detection\"; prompt \"Model and bypass multiple synthetic root signals\n28\twithout globally patching success\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec `base64` (4th time), debuggable false again. No root\n29\tprobe API (File/Build/Runtime.exec/su/magisk) in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `rootSignals` + `STRUCTURAL`.\n30\tFIRST 6-set Mastery (d01 plain, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d17 indexed, d22 base64).\n31\tD23 (Hook Line and Signal, `hook_detection` \"hook and instrumentation detection\"; prompt \"Separate real instrumentation\n32\tsignals from generated false positives\"): single = v1 `xor` (key 81). **TT and all 7 Mastery sets (d02, d06, d10, d14,\n33\td15, d22, d23 -- old days REGENERATED) shipped puzzle schema v2 `{\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..}` with NO data: the answer\n34\tis COMPUTED by dex code** -- `Release.code(Context)` = `\"ANS-\"` + 16 hex nibbles of a static 64-bit mixer chain\n35\t(`token()` = mixA(scanB(mixC(seed))); `scan*` folds in `Probe.s1/s2/s3` 12-bit inverse searches and a theme gate fn such\n36\tas `instrumentationSignals = (a^b^c)&7`; d14 set adds an LCG `long[16]` table walk; d15 set calls JNI `nativeShare(long)`\n37\tin `libarena.so`). Unreferenced look-alike mixers/`K*` consts = the \"generated false positives\". Solved by jadx +\n38\tjavac-with-Context-stub (LLM worker); the solver had no v2 path and `bytecode_vm_scan` resolved 2 of 8 v2 APKs.\n39\tD24 (Emulator Alibi, `emulator_detection` \"emulator environment detection\"; prompt \"Defeat app-owned environment checks on\n40\tthe same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle\"): single = v1 `split` (`parts[3]` + `order [2,0,1]`). TT + FIRST 8-set\n41\tMastery (d03, d06, d09, d10, d15, d17, d23, d24) all v2 `analysis`, same shape as D23: theme = gate fn\n42\t`EmulatorAlibi.emulatorScore(a,b,c) = (a+b+c)%4` over `Probe.s*` ints, decoys `sealEmu*`/`KQemu*`; NO Build/qemu/sensor/\n43\ttelephony API in any dex. The overnight v2 evaluator (lib deep Dalvik eval + solve.py unicorn JNI hop) solved all three\n44\tmodes first try (single 16.3 s via race probe, TT 2.5 s, Mastery 3.1 s).\n45\tD25 (Integrity Signals, `integrity_signal` \"challenge-owned integrity statement\"; prompt \"Forge or replay a bounded\n46\tchallenge-owned integrity statement and explain the missing binding\" -- Play Integrity nonce/requestHash pun): single =\n47\tv1 `hex`. TT = v2 with gate `IntegritySignals.integrityStatement(long,int) = a ^ (long)b` (first `(JI)J` gate; only 2\n48\tprobe calls), classes `SealCheck`/`VerdictMap`, decoys `KSeal*`/`KStatement*`/`KCert*`; NO PackageManager/signature/\n49\tIntegrityManager/token code. FIRST 9-set Mastery (d01, d04, d07, d10, d14, d16, d19, d22, d25), all v2, and the old-day\n50\tsets now carry their REAL mechanic: d19 set = `Class.forName`/`getDeclaredMethod`/`Method.invoke` dispatch picking 1 of\n51\t8 `Maze.mN(long)` via a packed-switch `dispatch(int)`; d16 set = `native nativeShare(long,int)` with the u16\n52\tlength-narrowing gate in the export. Solver 3/3 first try (single ~5 s race probe, TT 2.2 s, Mastery 3.7 s; Mastery solve\n53\t1.89 s, double D24's).\n54\tSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day; through D22 no exploit was ever needed. D23-D24 TT/Mastery\n55\tcompute the answer in code: assume the timed builds evaluate code, and that tomorrow's theme becomes a gate\n56\tfn / probe set INSIDE the v2 chain (the d10/d14/d22 sets already carry `gateDomain*`/`gateStream*` theme fns).\n57\tD15-D22 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation + decoys -> string\n58\tencryption -> reflection -> dynamic code loading -> anti-debug -> root detection -> hook (D23) -> emulator (D24) -> Play Integrity verdict (D25)).\n59\tStill unnamed in that arc: tamper/repackaging/installer, key attestation (D22's title pun is\n60\tthe attestation `RootOfTrust` ASN.1 record), certificate pinning checks, then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box crypto). After it the untouched MASVS\n61\tgroups are AUTH (biometric/local auth) and the leftover IPC surfaces (bound Service/AIDL, broadcast receivers).\n62\tNext expect also: the payload ENCRYPTED/wrapped (key in host dex, unwrap by\n63\tmagic known plaintext), \"challenge-signed\" made real (several payloads, only the one whose digest/signature matches a\n64\tpinned value is loaded), >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host-named member (`moduleContract`) deciding, class shadowing\n65\tbetween host and payload loaders, multi-stage loaders, anti-tamper / root / emulator / debugger / Frida checks, and\n66\tcontrol-flow flattening or a tiny VM. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection, d20\n67\tdynamic) and old ones recur (d18 xor, d21 reverse): check `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name, then decode from `ANS-` alone.\n68\t\