x-compose (`ans_compose_scan` returns decoys) | high |\n183\t| 99 | Chain reading Android state (assets JSON `build`, PackageManager signatures, Resources/arsc, SharedPreferences, `Build.*`, `Settings.Secure`) | gap (D23 `Release` stores the Context in a static but never reads it) | value depends on the APK's own bytes/facts via Context APIs | `ctx`/`getAssets`/`getPackageManager`/`getResources`/`JSONObject` in the chain | `analysis-android-api-stubs` prebuild (stubs answer from the APK + clean retail device) | high: why else pass a Context |\n184\t| 100 | Old-day mechanic regenerated as EXECUTABLE code inside a v2 Mastery set (the source day's API really called) | seen D25 (d19 set real reflection; d16 set native u16 gate); d14 LCG table and d15 JNI hop since D23 | the one link of the chain that uses the source day's API; rest is the usual mixer chain | JSON `day` != today, dex refs to the source day's API (`forName`, `loadLibrary`, `DexClassLoader`, `decryptByte`, `getSharedPreferences`, `SQLiteDatabase`, `KeyStore`, `isDebuggerConnected`) | deep evaluator; if silent on one set: `strings -a classes.dex` for that API, hand-eval the one link, batch-submit the rest | certain: 8 old days never yet v2 (d05 d08 d11 d12 d13 d18 d20 d21) |\n185\t| 101 | Cross-dex call from the v2 chain into `assets/payload.dex` (DexClassLoader / InMemoryDexClassLoader + loadClass + getMethod.invoke) | gap (D20 v1 only) | a static long fn in the payload dex invoked mid-chain | host dex refs `DexClassLoader`/`InMemoryDexClassLoader`/`getCodeCacheDir`/`getAssets().open`, payload class name string | `v2-dexloader-payload-invoke` prebuild; manual: jadx both dexes, javac them together with the Context stub | high: d20 set as v2 is due in Mastery |\n186\t\n187\t## Recognition cues (worker quick-reference)\n188\t\n189\t```\n190\t0. Always first: unzip -p x.apk assets/huntress_puzzle.json   (triage.md prints it)\n191\t   v1 {\"codec\":..,\"data\":..} -> python3 -c \"from lib.android import extract_answer as e;print(e('x.apk'))\"; submit ANS-...\n192\t   v2 {\"schema\":\"...v2\",\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..} NO data (D23-D25 TT + every Mastery set) -> answer is COMPUTED:\n193\t   run solve.py / lib.android.puzzle_candidates first (D24, D25: 3/3 modes, <2 s); by hand only if silent: step 5a.\n194\t   Prompt verbs (D24 \"pinned emulator\", D25 \"forge or replay an integrity statement\") have NOT meant live work: the\n195\t   theme is one pure gate fn in the chain. Nothing to forge, replay or emulate unless the dex really calls such APIs.\n196\t   Never chase 127.0.0.1:19090 (device loopback). Never submit a regex-composed ANS- (hex table + dead mixers = decoys).\n197\t1. unzip -l x.apk   -> map the entries:\n198\t   assets/huntress_puzzle.json      v1 codec; data already ANS-? done (D15 native, D19 reflection); new name -> data[:4] vs \"ANS-\"\n199\t                                    data = an entry path (D20 `dynamic`)? open THAT entry, recurse. int list (D5/D17): r[order[i]]=data[i]\n200\t   lib/<abi>/*.so                   strings -a | grep ANS- ; nm -D --defined-only ; no Java_* -> JNI_OnLoad/RegisterNatives\n201\t                                    D16 gate Java_*_native*(int)+*_accepts: objdump -d (bypass len 65536)\n202\t                                    D23 v2 d15 set: Java_*_nativeShare(long) called MID-CHAIN, pure arithmetic: port or unicorn\n203\t   lib/*/libapp.so + libflutter.so  Flutter: strings libapp.so; flutter_assets/kernel_blob.bin (debug = source text)\n204\t   assets/index.android.bundle      RN: head -c8 | xxd; c61fbc03 = Hermes -> hbc-decompiler; else webcrack/js-beautify\n205\t   assemblies/*.dll|*.blob, libmonodroid.so   Xamarin: XALZ = lz4 per-dll; then ilspycmd f.dll\n206\t   libil2cpp.so + global-metadata.dat         Unity IL2CPP: strings global-metadata.dat | grep ANS-\n207\t   assets/www/, cordova.js, capacitor.config  hybrid JS: grep -r in assets/www\n208\t   assets/*.dex|*.jar|*.apk|*.zip|*.bin       dynamic code (D20 plain dex): strings -a first; no dex/PK/ELF magic -> known-\n209\t                                    plaintext unwrap; >1 payload -> host's pinned digest; >1 ANS- -> member the host names\n210\t   libjiagu/libsecexe/libDexHelper.so          packer: payload is the encrypted asset; static decrypt or give up early\n211\t   res/xml/network_security_config.xml / resources.arsc   aapt dump xmltree ... ; aapt dump --values resources x.apk"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b5a4874-41a3-4f1d-b581-92bd56f6f405","uuid":"781f8223-98c8-43ce-a832-1df86c6ad96a","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:05:11.220Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/0b5a4874-41a3-4f1d-b581-92bd56f6f405/tool-results/bvq0736rj.txt","content":"# mobile-android: coverage atlas (D1-D25 seen, D26+ forecast)\n\nScope: common Android/mobile CTF concepts mapped against what this lane has shipped and what the harness can handle.\nGround truth (see `reference/techniques/mobile-android.md`): all 25 days shipped the same ~12.7 KB fixture. The day's\nTHEME was flavour only (manifest `huntress.mechanic` + dex `DAY-NN:<theme>:<mechanic>`). The answer `ANS-<16 HEX>` was\nin `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` behind a rotating codec (plain/reverse/base64/xor/split/hex/caesar/native/indexed/\nreflection) on D1-D19. D15\nadded the first real extra payload (`lib/x86_64/libarena.so` with the answer as a `.rodata` literal) and mixed-day\nMastery. D16 (JNI Boundary) TT/Mastery builds added the first REAL gate in code: `Java_<pkg>_JNIBoundary_nativeEvidence(int\nlen)` returns `arena_value` only if `len > 0xffff && (u16)len == 0` -- still with the literal in the asset and `.rodata`.\nD17 (Name Collapse, R8-style identifier collapse) left the native track: 6-entry fixture, new per-char permutation codec\n`indexed`, one renamed class `a`; the TT dex carried the real hint `follow b -> a and ignore field c` + `decoy` strings.\nD18 (Encrypted Strings, `string_decryption` \"runtime string decryption\"): 6-entry fixture, codec `xor` again (b64 + 1-byte\nkey); single dex had no cipher code, the TT/Mastery dex added class `EncryptedStrings` method `decryptByte` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nD19 (Reflection Maze, `reflective_dispatch` \"reflective secret dispatch\"; prompt \"Reconstruct reflective dispatch across\ngenerated equivalent call graphs\"): 6-entry fixture, NEW codec name `reflection` whose `data` is the plaintext answer;\nclass `ReflectionMaze`, but NO reflection API in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `dispatch` + `STRUCTURAL` strings.\nD20 (Loaded Later, `dynamic_dex` \"secondary DEX loading\"; prompt \"Analyze a challenge-signed secondary DEX and recover\nthe module contract\"): 7-entry APK with `assets/payload.dex` (508 B, plain dex 035); NEW codec `dynamic` whose `data` is\nthe ENTRY PATH `assets/payload.dex` -- the FIRST day the answer left the JSON value: a plain `ANS-` const in payload class\n`com.huntress.arena.payload.Module` (strings `ANSWER`, `CONTRACT`, `DAY20-SIGNED-MODULE:..`). No ClassLoader/verify code\nin any host dex; TT/Mastery host dex added `moduleContract` + `assets/payload.dex:com.huntress.arena.payload.Module`.\nD21 (Debug Me If You Can, `anti_debug` \"anti-debug state checks\"; prompt \"Neutralize a clean-room anti-debug state machine\nwhile retaining the intended app flow\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec back to `reverse` (d2/d8) -- the D20 pointer did\nNOT persist. First manifest with `android:debuggable=\"true\"` (single/TT/Mastery-d21 only). No debugger/TracerPid/clock\nAPI and no state loop in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `debuggerGate` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nD22 (Root of Trust, `root_detection` \"synthetic root detection\"; prompt \"Model and bypass multiple synthetic root signals\nwithout globally patching success\"): plain 6-entry fixture, codec `base64` (4th time), debuggable false again. No root\nprobe API (File/Build/Runtime.exec/su/magisk) in any dex; TT/Mastery dex only added `rootSignals` + `STRUCTURAL`.\nFIRST 6-set Mastery (d01 plain, d07 caesar, d12 hex, d13 base64, d17 indexed, d22 base64).\nD23 (Hook Line and Signal, `hook_detection` \"hook and instrumentation detection\"; prompt \"Separate real instrumentation\nsignals from generated false positives\"): single = v1 `xor` (key 81). **TT and all 7 Mastery sets (d02, d06, d10, d14,\nd15, d22, d23 -- old days REGENERATED) shipped puzzle schema v2 `{\"codec\":\"analysis\",\"build\":..}` with NO data: the answer\nis COMPUTED by dex code** -- `Release.code(Context)` = `\"ANS-\"` + 16 hex nibbles of a static 64-bit mixer chain\n(`token()` = mixA(scanB(mixC(seed))); `scan*` folds in `Probe.s1/s2/s3` 12-bit inverse searches and a theme gate fn such\nas `instrumentationSignals = (a^b^c)&7`; d14 set adds an LCG `long[16]` table walk; d15 set calls JNI `nativeShare(long)`\nin `libarena.so`). Unreferenced look-alike mixers/`K*` consts = the \"generated false positives\". Solved by jadx +\njavac-with-Context-stub (LLM worker); the solver had no v2 path and `bytecode_vm_scan` resolved 2 of 8 v2 APKs.\nD24 (Emulator Alibi, `emulator_detection` \"emulator environment detection\"; prompt \"Defeat app-owned environment checks on\nthe same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle\"): single = v1 `split` (`parts[3]` + `order [2,0,1]`). TT + FIRST 8-set\nMastery (d03, d06, d09, d10, d15, d17, d23, d24) all v2 `analysis`, same shape as D23: theme = gate fn\n`EmulatorAlibi.emulatorScore(a,b,c) = (a+b+c)%4` over `Probe.s*` ints, decoys `sealEmu*`/`KQemu*`; NO Build/qemu/sensor/\ntelephony API in any dex. The overnight v2 evaluator (lib deep Dalvik eval + solve.py unicorn JNI hop) solved all three\nmodes first try (single 16.3 s via race probe, TT 2.5 s, Mastery 3.1 s).\nD25 (Integrity Signals, `integrity_signal` \"challenge-owned integrity statement\"; prompt \"Forge or replay a bounded\nchallenge-owned integrity statement and explain the missing binding\" -- Play Integrity nonce/requestHash pun): single =\nv1 `hex`. TT = v2 with gate `IntegritySignals.integrityStatement(long,int) = a ^ (long)b` (first `(JI)J` gate; only 2\nprobe calls), classes `SealCheck`/`VerdictMap`, decoys `KSeal*`/`KStatement*`/`KCert*`; NO PackageManager/signature/\nIntegrityManager/token code. FIRST 9-set Mastery (d01, d04, d07, d10, d14, d16, d19, d22, d25), all v2, and the old-day\nsets now carry their REAL mechanic: d19 set = `Class.forName`/`getDeclaredMethod`/`Method.invoke` dispatch picking 1 of\n8 `Maze.mN(long)` via a packed-switch `dispatch(int)`; d16 set = `native nativeShare(long,int)` with the u16\nlength-narrowing gate in the export. Solver 3/3 first try (single ~5 s race probe, TT 2.2 s, Mastery 3.7 s; Mastery solve\n1.89 s, double D24's).\nSo \"seen Dn\" below means the THEME was named that day; through D22 no exploit was ever needed. D23-D24 TT/Mastery\ncompute the answer in code: assume the timed builds evaluate code, and that tomorrow's theme becomes a gate\nfn / probe set INSIDE the v2 chain (the d10/d14/d22 sets already carry `gateDomain*`/`gateStream*` theme fns).\nD15-D22 read as a MASVS-RESILIENCE / obfuscation arc (native secret -> JNI gate -> name obfuscation + decoys -> string\nencryption -> reflection -> dynamic code loading -> anti-debug -> root detection -> hook (D23) -> emulator (D24) -> Play Integrity verdict (D25)).\nStill unnamed in that arc: tamper/repackaging/installer, key attestation (D22's title pun is\nthe attestation `RootOfTrust` ASN.1 record), certificate pinning checks, then obfuscation capstones (flattening, VM, white-box crypto). After it the untouched MASVS\ngroups are AUTH (biometric/local auth) and the leftover IPC surfaces (bound Service/AIDL, broadcast receivers).\nNext expect also: the payload ENCRYPTED/wrapped (key in host dex, unwrap by\nmagic known plaintext), \"challenge-signed\" made real (several payloads, only the one whose digest/signature matches a\npinned value is loaded), >1 `ANS-` in the payload with the host-named member (`moduleContract`) deciding, class shadowing\nbetween host and payload loaders, multi-stage loaders, anti-tamper / root / emulator / debugger / Frida checks, and\ncontrol-flow flattening or a tiny VM. New codecs keep arriving (d7 caesar, d15 native, d17 indexed, d19 reflection, d20\ndynamic) and old ones recur (d18 xor, d21 reverse): check `data` for `ANS-`, then for an entry name, then decode from `ANS-` alone.\n\nTool status (after `source bin/env.sh`; checked 2026-10-15). INSTALLED: jadx 1.5.6, apktool 3.0.3, aapt, aapt2,\napksigner, keytool, jarsigner, d2j-dex2jar (+ `tools/dex2jar/d2j-*.sh`: baksmali, decrypt-string, ...), droidasc,\nandroguard (CLI + py), apkInspector, rizin/rz-bin, r2/rabin2, Ghidra `analyzeHeadless`, readelf/nm/strings, hbc-decompiler/\nhbc-disassembler/hbc-file-parser (hermes-dec), ilspycmd + dotnet, webcrack, js-beautify, sqlite3, 7z, binwalk, yara,\ntshark, zlib-flate, openssl, adb (no device). py: lief, pyelftools, capstone, unicorn, pycryptodome, lz4, plistlib.\nMISSING: blutter, reFlutter, pyxamstore, Il2CppDumper/Cpp2IL, frida/frida-tools/objection, apkid, apkleaks, bundletool,\nabe (android-backup-extractor), standalone baksmali/smali, dexdump, zipalign, de4dot, ipsw/plistutil/class-dump.\nTimed constraint: `solve.py` may use only stdlib + lib.* + pyzipper/pyelftools/pefile/capstone/pycryptodome/androguard,\nno subprocess, <1 s per set. Prebuilt extractors must be pure python.\n\n## Concept table\n\nLegend: tool `[i]` = installed here, `[M]` = missing. \"puzzle\" = `assets/huntress_puzzle.json` (`lib.android.puzzle_candidates`).\n\n| # | concept | status | where the answer likely hides | recognition cues | standard tool + exact command | D22+ likelihood |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Exported Activity / implicit-export default | seen D1 | puzzle; real CTFs: `onCreate` reveals the flag when started with a magic extra | `android:exported=\"true\"`, intent-filter w/o `exported` + targetSdk<31 | `aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml` [i]; `droidasc getmanifest x.apk` [i]; `lib.android.manifest_facts` | high: Mastery mixes old days |\n| 2 | Exported Service / AIDL / Messenger | gap | `onBind`/`onStartCommand`/`handleMessage` compares + returns secret | `<service exported>`, `extends Binder`, `$Stub`, `IInterface`, `Messenger` | `jadx -d out x.apk` [i]; `droidasc findrefs x.apk type Landroid/os/Binder;` | med: next IPC theme |\n| 3 | Broadcast receiver (exported, dynamic, ordered/sticky) | gap | `onReceive` action/extra check; action strings in dex | `<receiver exported>`, `registerReceiver`, `sendOrderedBroadcast`, custom `ACTION_*` | `aapt dump xmltree ...`; `jadx` grep `onReceive` | med-high: classic unused IPC theme |\n| 4 | Content provider (SQLi, path traversal, FileProvider paths) | seen D6 | puzzle; real: `query()` / `openFile()`, `res/xml/*paths*.xml` | `<provider exported grantUriPermissions>`, `UriMatcher`, `<root-path>`, `../` | `apktool d -f -o out x.apk` [i]; `aapt dump xmltree x.apk res/xml/file_paths.xml` | med (mixed Mastery) |\n| 5 | Custom permission weakness (normal level, typo, missing) | gap | manifest | `<permission protectionLevel=\"normal\">`, `android:permission` on comp vs `uses-permission` | `aapt dump permissions x.apk` [i] | med |\n| 6 | Task hijacking / StrandHogg | gap | manifest attrs (answer = static) | `taskAffinity`, `allowTaskReparenting=\"true\"`, `launchMode=\"singleTask\"` | `aapt dump xmltree ... \\| grep -E 'taskAffinity\\|launchMode\\|Reparent'` | med |\n| 7 | Tapjacking / overlay | gap | layout XML or manifest | `filterTouchesWhenObscured`, `FLAG_WINDOW_IS_OBSCURED`, `SYSTEM_ALERT_WINDOW` | `apktool d` then `grep -r filterTouches out/res` | med |\n| 8 | Deep link (custom scheme, param parsing) | seen D2 | puzzle; real: `getQueryParameter` branch | `<data android:scheme=..>`, `getData()`, `getQueryParameter` | `droidasc findrefs x.apk string <scheme>` [i]; `jadx` | high (mixed) |\n| 9 | App Links / autoVerify / assetlinks | gap | host + cert SHA-256 (assetlinks n