{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_011VRGk737TWwSVczCrJjoSU","type":"tool_result","content":"212\t   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n213\t   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem|*.der  keystore (password = dex string) / attestation cert: openssl x509 -inform DER -text\n214\t   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n215\t2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16): for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n216\t   7z l vs unzip -l differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n217\t3. Manifest: aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E 'exported|scheme|host|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|\n218\t   usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|meta-data'   (meta-data huntress.mechanic = theme; debuggable D21 = fact only)\n219\t4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY|CODEC|CONTROL|STRUCTURAL|ANS-' then map API hits to themes:\n220\t   DexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex      SecretKeySpec/Cipher -> static key decrypt     loadLibrary -> .so\n221\t   Random/setSeed -> regenerate RNG                MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash                   Binder/onReceive -> IPC\n222\t   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/debuggerGate/rootSignals/hook_detection -> clean_device_scan, clean value PER\n223\t   signal; never force the aggregate isRooted()/success flag. Class.forName -> reflection_scan. $SwitchMap$ /\n224\t   packed-switch loop -> flattened_cfg_scan. CertificatePinner -> pins. KeyStore BKS/PKCS12 -> res/raw keystore.\n225\t5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n226\t5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n227\t   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n228\t   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). Theme gate = 1 pure fn (D24 emulatorScore=(a+b+c)%4): no device to fake. FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n229\t   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n230\t   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n231\t   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n232\t   Old-day sets carry their mechanic as REAL code (D25): d19 set Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod(\"m\"+dispatch(k))\n233\t   .invoke -> follow only the named Maze.mN; d16 set native nativeShare(long,int) gates on (u16)len -> use the dex's\n234\t   own int arg. Expect d20 DexClassLoader payload, d18 decryptByte, d21 debugger state loop, d11 prefs next.\n235\t   v1-era hints: R8 \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" (D17); decryptByte (D18): eval the helper with call-site args.\n236\t6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n237\t   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n238\t7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n239\t8. Mastery: each set = different day AND maybe different schema (D23-D25: all v2; D25 9 sets); decode each APK alone;\n240\t   loop all answer_ids; one silent set -> hand-solve it, but batch-submit every answer in one request.\n241\t```\n242\t\n243\t## Readiness gaps\n244\t\n245\tPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n246\t`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\n247\taab-proto-manifest-parse, analysis-android-api-stubs, analysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening,\n248\tanalysis-interface-signal-list-eval, analysis-keystore-cert-api-stubs, analysis-release-code-eval,\n249\tanalysis-self-integrity-stubs, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path,\n250\tapk-signing-block-payload, asset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims,\n251\tbinder-ontransact-code-map, biometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool,\n252\tcert-and-signing-facts, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs,\n253\tcustom-alphabet-decode, dalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel,\n254\tdecrypt-call-site-args-eval, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-eval-float-double-semantics, dex-eval-long-intrinsics,\n255\tdex-eval-native-bridge, dex-eval-pure-static-memo, dex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args,\n256\tdex-native-split-assembly, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve,\n257\temulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, entry-anchored-candidate-veto, entry-reachable-callgraph-rank,\n258\tenum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval, hermes-hbc-string-table,\n259\thook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\n260\tinstaller-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs, instrumentation-false-positive-env, integrity-derived-key,\n261\tjava-serialized-object-parse, jni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, jni-reflection-callback,\n262\tjwt-token-decode-verify, key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse, known-string-obfuscator-signatures,\n263\tkotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, kotlin-object-chain-eval, messagedigest-derived-answer,\n264\tmodule-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native, multi-stage-loader-recurse, native-gated-branch-read,\n265\tnative-init-array-decrypt, native-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate, native-payload-system-load,\n266\tnative-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs, nested-container-recurse,\n267\topaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select, payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap,\n268\tpermutation-transposition-family, play-integrity-verdict-select, probe-arg-resolve-before-stub,\n269\tprocess-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\n270\tproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\n271\treflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family,\n272\troot-signal-vector-key, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt, static-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs,\n273\ttiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan, v1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan,\n274\twhitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack, zip-structure-anomaly-scan.\n275\t\n276\tForecast after D25: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc keeps naming one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook,\n277\tD24 emulator, D25 Play Integrity verdict) and the TT chain absorbs each as one pure gate fn (D25 only changed the gate\n278\tsignature to `(long,int)->long` and dropped to 2 probes). The real escalation moved into Mastery: regenerated OLD days\n279\tnow execute their own mechanic (D25 d19 real reflection, d16 native u16 gate). Mastery picks one old day per 3-day\n280\tstride and +1 set/day (D26 ~10 sets); never-yet-v2 days d05, d08, d11, d12, d13, d18, d20, d21 are due -- d20\n281\t(DexClassLoader payload), d18 (decryptByte strings) and d21 (debugger state loop) are the costly ones. Still unnamed\n282\tfor D26-D31 (6 days left): anti-tamper / repackaging / signature, certificate pinning, key attestation, then obfuscation\n283\tcapstones (flattening, VM, white-box) and probably a final all-days capstone. Mastery solve time doubled D24->D25\n284\t(0.94 -> 1.89 s): keep per-set cost flat as the bundle grows.\n285\t\n286\t```json[\n287\t  {\"id\": \"analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain\", \"concept\": \"certificate-pinning theme in the v2 chain: SPKI SHA-256 pins computed from a shipped cert and compared / folded (rows 27, 28, 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pinning (D9 trust manager, D10 NSC) has only been flavour; a resilience-arc 'pinning bypass' day would compute `sha256/` + base64(SHA-256(SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER)) of res/raw|assets cert(s) and compare to the NSC `<pin digest=\\\"SHA-256\\\">` / OkHttp CertificatePinner string, folding the match index or the digest bytes into the seed. Provide: SPKI extraction from X.509 DER (asn1 walk, no openssl subprocess), Base64.encodeToString flags (NO_WRAP/DEFAULT newline), MessageDigest intrinsics, NSC pin-set parse from res/xml (binary XML via aapt-free lib parser), and expiry-date compare. Report which pin matched which cert.\"},\n288\t  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scaling-bench\", \"concept\": \"Mastery grows +1 set per day (5,6,7,8): keep every v2 set solvable inside the window as the bundle grows (row 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25: 9 sets took 1.89 s solve (D24 8 sets 0.94 s) -- the per-set cost roughly doubled with the new d19 reflection / d16 gated-native sets; find which set is slow first. D24 8 sets solved in 0.94 s (TT single set 0.39 s), with one forked process per set. At +1/day D31 could carry ~15 sets including several JNI/unicorn sets. Build a bench (tests or tools script, pure python) that runs the deep evaluator over every v2 fixture under challenges/day2[34]/**/cases and fails if any set > 0.4 s or the total of a 15-set synthetic bundle (fixtures repeated) > 3 s on one core; profile and fix hotspots (unicorn Uc construction per call -> cache per .so; dex parse per set -> cache by sha256; Probe inverse searches -> closed form when f is affine mod 4096).\"},\n289\t  {\"id\": \"v2-dexloader-payload-invoke\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain calls into a second dex: DexClassLoader / InMemoryDexClassLoader over assets/payload.dex + loadClass + getMethod/getDeclaredMethod.invoke (rows 42, 100, 101)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 showed regenerated old-day Mastery sets now RUN their mechanic (d19 real reflection). d20 (Loaded Later) has never been a v2 set; its mechanic is a secondary dex. Expect host code: `new DexClassLoader(path, ctx.getCodeCacheDir().getPath(), null, getClassLoader())` after copying `getAssets().open(\\\"payload.dex\\\")` to a file, or `new InMemoryDexClassLoader(ByteBuffer.wrap(bytes), parent)`; then `loadClass(\\\"com.huntress.arena.payload.Module\\\")` -> `getMethod(name, long.class).invoke(null, Long.valueOf(v))` -> unbox. Deep evaluator: model AssetManager.open/InputStream.read/readAllBytes/ByteArrayOutputStream/FileOutputStream as in-memory bytes from the APK entry, parse the payload dex (also xor/b64-wrapped: reuse payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap), register its classes in a second class table consulted by loadClass (parent-first: host classes win on name clash, per classloader-shadow-resolve), and continue evaluation inside it (static fields, <clinit>). Test with a synthetic chain built from the D20 payload.dex fixture.\"},\n290\t  {\"id\": \"v2-string-decrypt-name-resolve\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain decrypts its own strings (d18 decryptByte) and feeds them to reflection / class lookup / the hex table (rows 35, 43, 70, 100)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"d18 (Encrypted Strings) has never been a v2 set; combined with D25's real reflection, a regenerated d18 set would build method/class names or the `0123456789ABCDEF` table from byte[]/char[] arrays via `decryptByte(b, i)` (`b ^ k ^ i`, `(b - k) & 0xff`, key array cycled) then `new String(bytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8|US_ASCII|ISO_8859_1)`, `String.valueOf(char[])`, `new String(char[])`, `toCharArray`, `getBytes`, `intern`. Make the deep evaluator exact for: fill-array-data, byte sign extension (`int-to-byte`), char arithmetic (`int-to-char`), String(byte[], charset name or Charset object), StandardCharsets static fields, Charset.forName, String.format, then reflection lookups using the decrypted name. Regression: D18 TT dex helpers + a synthetic chain.\"},\n291\t  {\"id\": \"v2-debugger-gate-state-loop\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain with the d21 anti-debug mechanic as code: debuggerGate state machine (while/packed-switch) over Debug/ApplicationInfo/TracerPid/timing probes (rows 41, 79, 88, 100)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"d21 (Debug Me If You Can) has never been a v2 set; its theme words are 'clean-room anti-debug state machine while retaining the intended app flow'. Expect `int state = S0; while (state != DONE) switch (state) { ... }` with transitions on `Debug.isDebuggerConnected()`, `Debug.waitingForDebugger()`, `(ctx.getApplicationInfo().flags & FLAG_DEBUGGABLE) != 0` (D21 manifests set debuggable=true -> read the APK's OWN manifest flag, but the 'intended flow' is the non-debugged path: report both), `/proc/self/status` TracerPid read via BufferedReader(FileReader), `SystemClock.elapsedRealtime()` deltas. Evaluator: clean answers (false / TracerPid:\\\\t0 / small monotonic delta), a loop-iteration cap, and for ApplicationInfo.flags evaluate both manifest-true and clean-false, preferring the value that keeps the chain on its non-trap path (no -1/0 sentinel). Reuse anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path + flattened-cfg-switch-eval helpers inside _DxeDeepVM.\"},\n292\t  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n293\t  {\"id\": \"pinned-emulator-env-profile\", \"concept\": \"environment probes answered as the solve oracle's PINNED stock emulator, alongside the clean-Pixel profile (rows 48, 99)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 note: the emulator theme passed with no env read in any dex; first prebuild attempt failed (ok:false) -- retry once. D24 prompt: 'Defeat app-owned environment checks on the same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle' -- the reference answer is produced ON an emulator, so if a chain ever reads the environment, the clean-Pixel stubs (clean-device-env-stubs, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, analysis-android-api-stubs) may give the WRONG value. Add a second env profile to the deep evaluator and to clean_device_scan: a stock Google AVD x86_64 (Build.FINGERPRINT google/sdk_gphone64_x86_64/emu64x:14/...:userdebug/dev-keys, MODEL sdk_gphone64_x86_64, MANUFACTURER Google, BRAND google, HARDWARE ranchu, PRODUCT sdk_gphone64_x86_64, DEVICE emu64x, BOARD goldfish_x86_64, TAGS dev-keys, TYPE userdebug; ro.kernel.qemu=1, ro.boot.qemu=1, ro.hardware=ranchu, qemu.sf.lcd_density, /dev/qemu_pipe + /dev/goldfish_pipe present; TelephonyManager operator 'Android'/'310260', line1 15555215554, deviceId 358240051111110; sensor list with 'Goldfish 3-axis Accelerometer'; battery 50%/AC). Evaluate the entry under BOTH profiles; if the values differ, return both with labels (emulator first when the prompt says 'pinned emulator'/'solve oracle', clean first otherwise) and log which probe diverged. Keep the clean profile the default for v1 code-side scans.\"},\n294\t  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-java-random-lcg\", \"concept\": \"java.util.Random / SplittableRandom / ThreadLocalRandom-free determinism inside the v2 evaluator (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"First attempt failed (ok:false); d14 regenerated sets use an inline LCG table, not java.util.Random, so far. lib already carries the 0x5DEECE66D LCG for v1 scans; the deep evaluator (`_DxeDeepVM`) needs it as intrinsics: new Random(long) (seed ^ 0x5DEECE66D, 48-bit), nextInt(), nextInt(bound) incl. the power-of-two and rejection loop, nextLong(), nextBoolean(), nextDouble() (26+27 bits), nextBytes(byte[]), setSeed; java.util.SplittableRandom(seed).nextLong()/nextInt (mix64 / GOLDEN_GAMMA); Collections.shuffle(list, rnd); UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes (MD5). Unseeded new Random()/Math.random()/System.nanoTime -> report 'non-deterministic' and abort that candidate rather than invent a value.\"},\n295\t  {\"id\": \"native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks\", \"concept\": \"JNI export inside the v2 chain that calls back into JNIEnv (strings, static fields, Java methods) (rows 37, 82, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 d16 set added an int arg + u16 gate (`nativeShare(long,int)`) but still no JNIEnv use; first attempt failed (ok:false). D23/D24 d15 set `nativeShare(long)` is pure arithmetic; the next native step uses the env: GetStringUTFChars/ReleaseStringUTFChars on a jstring arg, NewStringUTF result, GetArrayLength/GetByteArrayElements/GetByteArrayRegion on a byte[] arg, FindClass + GetStaticFieldID + GetStaticLongField/GetStaticIntField (read a dex `K*` const), GetStaticMethodID + CallStaticLongMethod(A|V) back into a dex mixer. In solve.py-style unicorn harness (`_native_call`): build a real JNINativeInterface function table (229 slots, each a hook address), resolve each called slot by index, service it from the Dalvik evaluator (strings via a handle table, callbacks re-entering `_DxeDeepVM.run`), then resume. Support x86_64 and arm64-v8a. Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n296\t  {\"id\": \"v2-app-state-first-run-defaults\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain reading app-private state (SharedPreferences, SQLite, Keystore, backup flags) answered as a fresh install (rows 16-18, 31, 100)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"d05 (backup), d11 (SharedPreferences), d12 (SQLite) and d13 (Keystore) are due as v2 Mastery sets with their mechanic in code. Intrinsics for the deep evaluator: `ctx.getSharedPreferences(name, mode)` -> empty store whose getLong/getInt/getString/getBoolean return the DEFAULT arg, edit().putX().apply()/commit() then readable in the same run; `SQLiteOpenHelper`/`openOrCreateDatabase` + execSQL CREATE/INSERT + rawQuery/Cursor.moveToFirst/getLong/getString over a tiny in-memory sqlite3 (python stdlib) -- statements are dex const-strings; `KeyStore.getInstance(\\\"AndroidKeyStore\\\").load(null)`, containsAlias -> false on first run, `size()` 0; `ApplicationInfo.flags` FLAG_ALLOW_BACKUP (0x8000) / FLAG_USES_CLEARTEXT_TRAFFIC (0x8000000) / FLAG_DEBUGGABLE (2) from the APK's own manifest; `NetworkSecurityPolicy.getInstance().isCleartextTrafficPermitted(host)` from the NSC xml. Abort a candidate (not invent) on unmodelled state.\"},\n297\t  {\"id\": \"v2-reflection-api-breadth\", \"concept\": \"reflection variants beyond D25's forName+getDeclaredMethod+invoke inside the v2 evaluator (rows 43, 77, 80)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 d19 set: `\\\"m\\\"+dispatch(k)` -> Class.forName -> getDeclaredMethod(name, Long.TYPE) -> invoke(null, Long) -> check-cast Long -> longValue. Next generator steps: iterate `getDeclaredMethods()`/`getMethods()` filtering on getName().equals/hashCode()/startsWith or on an annotation, `Method.getParameterTypes().length`, `getDeclaredField(name).getLong(null)` / `Field.setAccessible(true)`, `getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance()` + instance invoke, `Class.getName()/getSimpleName()` used as hash input, `MethodHandles.lookup().findStatic(cls, name, MethodType.methodType(long.class, long.class)).invokeExact(v)`, `Integer.TYPE` vs `Integer.class` boxing, InvocationTargetException wrapping. Define dex method/field ORDER as declared-order (dex class_data order) and document it; sort-sensitive generators may rely on it.\"},\n298\t  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n299\t  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n300\t  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n301\t  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: hand-solved TT/Mastery left solve.py without a v2 path; the overnight prebuild fixed it and D24 went 3/3 on the solver alone. Keep the rule: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish offline and require `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json.\"},\n302\t  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n303\t  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n304\t  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n305\t  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n306\t  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n307\t  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n308\t]\n309\t```\n310\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b5a4874-41a3-4f1d-b581-92bd56f6f405","uuid":"56b57c2e-4102-4eb1-81f3-20044b023ad6","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:05:14.144Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/testpwn/.claude/projects/-home-testpwn-huntress-2026/0b5a4874-41a3-4f1d-b581-92bd56f6f405/tool-results/bvq0736rj.txt","content":"   *.db / shared_prefs/*.xml / *.ab sqlite3 f.db .dump ; .ab: dd bs=24 skip=1 | zlib-flate -uncompress | tar x\n   res/raw/*.bks|*.p12|*.pem|*.der  keystore (password = dex string) / attestation cert: openssl x509 -inform DER -text\n   base.apk + split_config.*.apk / toc.pb / BundleConfig.pb   split/XAPK/APKS/AAB: unzip inner, recurse\n2. Plain-anywhere scan (incl. UTF-16): for f in $(unzip -Z1 x.apk); do unzip -p x.apk \"$f\" | strings -a -el | grep -H --label=\"$f\" ANS-; done\n   7z l vs unzip -l differ -> zip tricks (dup entry / trailing data): binwalk x.apk\n3. Manifest: aapt dump xmltree x.apk AndroidManifest.xml | grep -E 'exported|scheme|host|permission|debuggable|allowBackup|\n   usesCleartext|networkSecurity|taskAffinity|meta-data'   (meta-data huntress.mechanic = theme; debuggable D21 = fact only)\n4. Dex triage: strings -a classes*.dex | grep -E 'DAY|CODEC|CONTROL|STRUCTURAL|ANS-' then map API hits to themes:\n   DexClassLoader/moduleContract -> asset dex      SecretKeySpec/Cipher -> static key decrypt     loadLibrary -> .so\n   Random/setSeed -> regenerate RNG                MessageDigest/PBKDF2 -> hash                   Binder/onReceive -> IPC\n   su/magisk/goldfish/frida/TracerPid/debuggerGate/rootSignals/hook_detection -> clean_device_scan, clean value PER\n   signal; never force the aggregate isRooted()/success flag. Class.forName -> reflection_scan. $SwitchMap$ /\n   packed-switch loop -> flattened_cfg_scan. CertificatePinner -> pins. KeyStore BKS/PKCS12 -> res/raw keystore.\n5. Code (after 1-4): jadx -q -d w/j x.apk (--deobf for 1-letter names); droidasc getclass x.apk <cls>\n5a. v2 `analysis` (D23): find what ChallengeActivity appends before `proof=` (Release.code(ctx)); token() = nested static\n   long fns from a const-wide seed; Probe.s1/s2/s3 = <=4096-step inverse searches; theme gate fn (x^y^z)&7 etc.;\n   Tab.build LCG long[16] walk (D14 set). Theme gate = 1 pure fn (D24 emulatorScore=(a+b+c)%4): no device to fake. FAST: copy non-Activity sources, add `package android.content; public class\n   Context {}`, Main prints Release.code(null), javac + java (D23: 7 sets in ~1.5 min). native method -> stub prints its\n   input, compute the export (objdump -d; port to py), feed back. Unreferenced seal*/K* members = decoys. Python port:\n   mask 2^64, `>>>` logical, signed->unsigned before rotate. In solve.py: lib Dalvik evaluator on Release.code only.\n   Old-day sets carry their mechanic as REAL code (D25): d19 set Class.forName/getDeclaredMethod(\"m\"+dispatch(k))\n   .invoke -> follow only the named Maze.mN; d16 set native nativeShare(long,int) gates on (u16)len -> use the dex's\n   own int arg. Expect d20 DexClassLoader payload, d18 decryptByte, d21 debugger state loop, d11 prefs next.\n   v1-era hints: R8 \"follow b -> a and ignore field c\" (D17); decryptByte (D18): eval the helper with call-site args.\n6. Native, if no literal: rizin -A -qc 'iE; izz~ANS; afl' f.so ; pdf @ sym.Java_... ; xor loops -> py capstone/unicorn.\n   NEVER ctypes.CDLL / dlopen an artifact .so on the host (sandbox rule) -- emulate or port.\n7. Validate: fullmatch ^ANS-[0-9A-F]{16}$ (uppercase). v2: also Release.proof == Long.toHexString(token) consistency.\n8. Mastery: each set = different day AND maybe different schema (D23-D25: all v2; D25 9 sets); decode each APK alone;\n   loop all answer_ids; one silent set -> hand-solve it, but batch-submit every answer in one request.\n```\n\n## Readiness gaps\n\nPriority 1 = plausible within ~3 days. \"prebuild\" = pure-python extractor in `lib/android.py` style that races in\n`solve.py`. \"tool\" = install. \"note\" = doc/prompt change. Already built or given up (prebuild-state ok / attempts>=2, dropped from the list):\naab-proto-manifest-parse, analysis-android-api-stubs, analysis-chain-obfuscation-hardening,\nanalysis-interface-signal-list-eval, analysis-keystore-cert-api-stubs, analysis-release-code-eval,\nanalysis-self-integrity-stubs, ans-prefix-numeric-compose, anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path,\napk-signing-block-payload, asset-cipher-dex-loader, asset-db-prefs-backup, attestation-jws-claims,\nbinder-ontransact-code-map, biometric-auth-callback-eval, broadcast-receiver-action-map, cdex-vdex-string-pool,\ncert-and-signing-facts, cert-pin-and-nsc-facts, classloader-shadow-resolve, clean-device-env-stubs,\ncustom-alphabet-decode, dalvik-mini-interpreter, dart-snapshot-string-pool, decode-any-chain-peel,\ndecrypt-call-site-args-eval, dex-bytecode-integrity-gate, dex-eval-float-double-semantics, dex-eval-long-intrinsics,\ndex-eval-native-bridge, dex-eval-pure-static-memo, dex-gated-branch-consts, dex-native-call-args,\ndex-native-split-assembly, dex-slack-and-header-anomaly, dex-string-decrypt-arrays, dispatch-key-resolve,\nemulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, entry-anchored-candidate-veto, entry-reachable-callgraph-rank,\nenum-switchmap-state-resolve, exception-driven-control-flow, flattened-cfg-switch-eval, hermes-hbc-string-table,\nhook-framework-introspection-stubs, identifier-collision-resolve, identity-derived-key, il2cpp-metadata-literals,\ninstaller-source-and-tamper-probe-stubs, instrumentation-false-positive-env, integrity-derived-key,\njava-serialized-object-parse, jni-export-return-trace, jni-gate-bypass-input, jni-reflection-callback,\njwt-token-decode-verify, key-attestation-rootoftrust-parse, known-string-obfuscator-signatures,\nkotlin-metadata-names-and-coroutines, kotlin-object-chain-eval, messagedigest-derived-answer,\nmodule-contract-member-eval, multi-abi-arm-native, multi-stage-loader-recurse, native-gated-branch-read,\nnative-init-array-decrypt, native-inline-syscall-stubs, native-libc-probe-stubs-emulate, native-payload-system-load,\nnative-so-emulate-export, native-stack-string, native-system-property-and-mounts-stubs, nested-container-recurse,\nopaque-predicate-dead-branch, payload-digest-pinned-select, payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap,\npermutation-transposition-family, play-integrity-verdict-select, probe-arg-resolve-before-stub,\nprocess-exec-shell-probe-stubs, proguard-mapping-restore, proof-flow-candidate-ranking, protobuf-asset-wire-decode,\nproxy-methodhandle-invokecustom, puzzle-entry-pointer-follow, puzzle-indexed-and-perm-fields, r8-renamed-chain-follow,\nreflection-name-resolve, registernatives-table, resource-id-const-resolve, rolling-xor-keystream-family,\nroot-signal-vector-key, sqlcipher-asset-decrypt, static-key-cipher-decode, timing-and-debug-flag-probe-stubs,\ntiny-bytecode-vm-interpret, utf16-string-pool-scan, v1-manifest-digest-verify, webview-asset-js-scan,\nwhitebox-table-cipher-eval, xamarin-xalz-blob-unpack, zip-structure-anomaly-scan.\n\nForecast after D25: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc keeps naming one control per day (D21 anti-debug, D22 root, D23 hook,\nD24 emulator, D25 Play Integrity verdict) and the TT chain absorbs each as one pure gate fn (D25 only changed the gate\nsignature to `(long,int)->long` and dropped to 2 probes). The real escalation moved into Mastery: regenerated OLD days\nnow execute their own mechanic (D25 d19 real reflection, d16 native u16 gate). Mastery picks one old day per 3-day\nstride and +1 set/day (D26 ~10 sets); never-yet-v2 days d05, d08, d11, d12, d13, d18, d20, d21 are due -- d20\n(DexClassLoader payload), d18 (decryptByte strings) and d21 (debugger state loop) are the costly ones. Still unnamed\nfor D26-D31 (6 days left): anti-tamper / repackaging / signature, certificate pinning, key attestation, then obfuscation\ncapstones (flattening, VM, white-box) and probably a final all-days capstone. Mastery solve time doubled D24->D25\n(0.94 -> 1.89 s): keep per-set cost flat as the bundle grows.\n\n```json[\n  {\"id\": \"analysis-cert-pin-digest-chain\", \"concept\": \"certificate-pinning theme in the v2 chain: SPKI SHA-256 pins computed from a shipped cert and compared / folded (rows 27, 28, 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"Pinning (D9 trust manager, D10 NSC) has only been flavour; a resilience-arc 'pinning bypass' day would compute `sha256/` + base64(SHA-256(SubjectPublicKeyInfo DER)) of res/raw|assets cert(s) and compare to the NSC `<pin digest=\\\"SHA-256\\\">` / OkHttp CertificatePinner string, folding the match index or the digest bytes into the seed. Provide: SPKI extraction from X.509 DER (asn1 walk, no openssl subprocess), Base64.encodeToString flags (NO_WRAP/DEFAULT newline), MessageDigest intrinsics, NSC pin-set parse from res/xml (binary XML via aapt-free lib parser), and expiry-date compare. Report which pin matched which cert.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"mastery-set-scaling-bench\", \"concept\": \"Mastery grows +1 set per day (5,6,7,8): keep every v2 set solvable inside the window as the bundle grows (row 96)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25: 9 sets took 1.89 s solve (D24 8 sets 0.94 s) -- the per-set cost roughly doubled with the new d19 reflection / d16 gated-native sets; find which set is slow first. D24 8 sets solved in 0.94 s (TT single set 0.39 s), with one forked process per set. At +1/day D31 could carry ~15 sets including several JNI/unicorn sets. Build a bench (tests or tools script, pure python) that runs the deep evaluator over every v2 fixture under challenges/day2[34]/**/cases and fails if any set > 0.4 s or the total of a 15-set synthetic bundle (fixtures repeated) > 3 s on one core; profile and fix hotspots (unicorn Uc construction per call -> cache per .so; dex parse per set -> cache by sha256; Probe inverse searches -> closed form when f is affine mod 4096).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"v2-dexloader-payload-invoke\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain calls into a second dex: DexClassLoader / InMemoryDexClassLoader over assets/payload.dex + loadClass + getMethod/getDeclaredMethod.invoke (rows 42, 100, 101)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 showed regenerated old-day Mastery sets now RUN their mechanic (d19 real reflection). d20 (Loaded Later) has never been a v2 set; its mechanic is a secondary dex. Expect host code: `new DexClassLoader(path, ctx.getCodeCacheDir().getPath(), null, getClassLoader())` after copying `getAssets().open(\\\"payload.dex\\\")` to a file, or `new InMemoryDexClassLoader(ByteBuffer.wrap(bytes), parent)`; then `loadClass(\\\"com.huntress.arena.payload.Module\\\")` -> `getMethod(name, long.class).invoke(null, Long.valueOf(v))` -> unbox. Deep evaluator: model AssetManager.open/InputStream.read/readAllBytes/ByteArrayOutputStream/FileOutputStream as in-memory bytes from the APK entry, parse the payload dex (also xor/b64-wrapped: reuse payload-magic-known-plaintext-unwrap), register its classes in a second class table consulted by loadClass (parent-first: host classes win on name clash, per classloader-shadow-resolve), and continue evaluation inside it (static fields, <clinit>). Test with a synthetic chain built from the D20 payload.dex fixture.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"v2-string-decrypt-name-resolve\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain decrypts its own strings (d18 decryptByte) and feeds them to reflection / class lookup / the hex table (rows 35, 43, 70, 100)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"d18 (Encrypted Strings) has never been a v2 set; combined with D25's real reflection, a regenerated d18 set would build method/class names or the `0123456789ABCDEF` table from byte[]/char[] arrays via `decryptByte(b, i)` (`b ^ k ^ i`, `(b - k) & 0xff`, key array cycled) then `new String(bytes, StandardCharsets.UTF_8|US_ASCII|ISO_8859_1)`, `String.valueOf(char[])`, `new String(char[])`, `toCharArray`, `getBytes`, `intern`. Make the deep evaluator exact for: fill-array-data, byte sign extension (`int-to-byte`), char arithmetic (`int-to-char`), String(byte[], charset name or Charset object), StandardCharsets static fields, Charset.forName, String.format, then reflection lookups using the decrypted name. Regression: D18 TT dex helpers + a synthetic chain.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"v2-debugger-gate-state-loop\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain with the d21 anti-debug mechanic as code: debuggerGate state machine (while/packed-switch) over Debug/ApplicationInfo/TracerPid/timing probes (rows 41, 79, 88, 100)\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"d21 (Debug Me If You Can) has never been a v2 set; its theme words are 'clean-room anti-debug state machine while retaining the intended app flow'. Expect `int state = S0; while (state != DONE) switch (state) { ... }` with transitions on `Debug.isDebuggerConnected()`, `Debug.waitingForDebugger()`, `(ctx.getApplicationInfo().flags & FLAG_DEBUGGABLE) != 0` (D21 manifests set debuggable=true -> read the APK's OWN manifest flag, but the 'intended flow' is the non-debugged path: report both), `/proc/self/status` TracerPid read via BufferedReader(FileReader), `SystemClock.elapsedRealtime()` deltas. Evaluator: clean answers (false / TracerPid:\\\\t0 / small monotonic delta), a loop-iteration cap, and for ApplicationInfo.flags evaluate both manifest-true and clean-false, preferring the value that keeps the chain on its non-trap path (no -1/0 sentinel). Reuse anti-debug-state-machine-clean-path + flattened-cfg-switch-eval helpers inside _DxeDeepVM.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"worker-cue-inline\", \"concept\": \"unseen-theme routing\", \"priority\": 1, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Inline the 'Recognition cues' block above into the mobile worker prompt (skills/huntress-ctf mobile skill) so an unseen container (Flutter/RN/Xamarin/asset dex) is routed in 1-2 turns; add step 2's UTF-16 scan to triage.md pre-extraction.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pinned-emulator-env-profile\", \"concept\": \"environment probes answered as the solve oracle's PINNED stock emulator, alongside the clean-Pixel profile (rows 48, 99)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 note: the emulator theme passed with no env read in any dex; first prebuild attempt failed (ok:false) -- retry once. D24 prompt: 'Defeat app-owned environment checks on the same pinned emulator used by the solve oracle' -- the reference answer is produced ON an emulator, so if a chain ever reads the environment, the clean-Pixel stubs (clean-device-env-stubs, emulator-telephony-sensor-stubs, analysis-android-api-stubs) may give the WRONG value. Add a second env profile to the deep evaluator and to clean_device_scan: a stock Google AVD x86_64 (Build.FINGERPRINT google/sdk_gphone64_x86_64/emu64x:14/...:userdebug/dev-keys, MODEL sdk_gphone64_x86_64, MANUFACTURER Google, BRAND google, HARDWARE ranchu, PRODUCT sdk_gphone64_x86_64, DEVICE emu64x, BOARD goldfish_x86_64, TAGS dev-keys, TYPE userdebug; ro.kernel.qemu=1, ro.boot.qemu=1, ro.hardware=ranchu, qemu.sf.lcd_density, /dev/qemu_pipe + /dev/goldfish_pipe present; TelephonyManager operator 'Android'/'310260', line1 15555215554, deviceId 358240051111110; sensor list with 'Goldfish 3-axis Accelerometer'; battery 50%/AC). Evaluate the entry under BOTH profiles; if the values differ, return both with labels (emulator first when the prompt says 'pinned emulator'/'solve oracle', clean first otherwise) and log which probe diverged. Keep the clean profile the default for v1 code-side scans.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"dex-eval-java-random-lcg\", \"concept\": \"java.util.Random / SplittableRandom / ThreadLocalRandom-free determinism inside the v2 evaluator (row 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"First attempt failed (ok:false); d14 regenerated sets use an inline LCG table, not java.util.Random, so far. lib already carries the 0x5DEECE66D LCG for v1 scans; the deep evaluator (`_DxeDeepVM`) needs it as intrinsics: new Random(long) (seed ^ 0x5DEECE66D, 48-bit), nextInt(), nextInt(bound) incl. the power-of-two and rejection loop, nextLong(), nextBoolean(), nextDouble() (26+27 bits), nextBytes(byte[]), setSeed; java.util.SplittableRandom(seed).nextLong()/nextInt (mix64 / GOLDEN_GAMMA); Collections.shuffle(list, rnd); UUID.nameUUIDFromBytes (MD5). Unseeded new Random()/Math.random()/System.nanoTime -> report 'non-deterministic' and abort that candidate rather than invent a value.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"native-bridge-jnienv-callbacks\", \"concept\": \"JNI export inside the v2 chain that calls back into JNIEnv (strings, static fields, Java methods) (rows 37, 82, 96)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 d16 set added an int arg + u16 gate (`nativeShare(long,int)`) but still no JNIEnv use; first attempt failed (ok:false). D23/D24 d15 set `nativeShare(long)` is pure arithmetic; the next native step uses the env: GetStringUTFChars/ReleaseStringUTFChars on a jstring arg, NewStringUTF result, GetArrayLength/GetByteArrayElements/GetByteArrayRegion on a byte[] arg, FindClass + GetStaticFieldID + GetStaticLongField/GetStaticIntField (read a dex `K*` const), GetStaticMethodID + CallStaticLongMethod(A|V) back into a dex mixer. In solve.py-style unicorn harness (`_native_call`): build a real JNINativeInterface function table (229 slots, each a hook address), resolve each called slot by index, service it from the Dalvik evaluator (strings via a handle table, callbacks re-entering `_DxeDeepVM.run`), then resume. Support x86_64 and arm64-v8a. Never dlopen the artifact.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"v2-app-state-first-run-defaults\", \"concept\": \"v2 chain reading app-private state (SharedPreferences, SQLite, Keystore, backup flags) answered as a fresh install (rows 16-18, 31, 100)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"d05 (backup), d11 (SharedPreferences), d12 (SQLite) and d13 (Keystore) are due as v2 Mastery sets with their mechanic in code. Intrinsics for the deep evaluator: `ctx.getSharedPreferences(name, mode)` -> empty store whose getLong/getInt/getString/getBoolean return the DEFAULT arg, edit().putX().apply()/commit() then readable in the same run; `SQLiteOpenHelper`/`openOrCreateDatabase` + execSQL CREATE/INSERT + rawQuery/Cursor.moveToFirst/getLong/getString over a tiny in-memory sqlite3 (python stdlib) -- statements are dex const-strings; `KeyStore.getInstance(\\\"AndroidKeyStore\\\").load(null)`, containsAlias -> false on first run, `size()` 0; `ApplicationInfo.flags` FLAG_ALLOW_BACKUP (0x8000) / FLAG_USES_CLEARTEXT_TRAFFIC (0x8000000) / FLAG_DEBUGGABLE (2) from the APK's own manifest; `NetworkSecurityPolicy.getInstance().isCleartextTrafficPermitted(host)` from the NSC xml. Abort a candidate (not invent) on unmodelled state.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"v2-reflection-api-breadth\", \"concept\": \"reflection variants beyond D25's forName+getDeclaredMethod+invoke inside the v2 evaluator (rows 43, 77, 80)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"prebuild\", \"detail\": \"D25 d19 set: `\\\"m\\\"+dispatch(k)` -> Class.forName -> getDeclaredMethod(name, Long.TYPE) -> invoke(null, Long) -> check-cast Long -> longValue. Next generator steps: iterate `getDeclaredMethods()`/`getMethods()` filtering on getName().equals/hashCode()/startsWith or on an annotation, `Method.getParameterTypes().length`, `getDeclaredField(name).getLong(null)` / `Field.setAccessible(true)`, `getDeclaredConstructor().newInstance()` + instance invoke, `Class.getName()/getSimpleName()` used as hash input, `MethodHandles.lookup().findStatic(cls, name, MethodType.methodType(long.class, long.class)).invokeExact(v)`, `Integer.TYPE` vs `Integer.class` boxing, InvocationTargetException wrapping. Define dex method/field ORDER as declared-order (dex class_data order) and document it; sort-sensitive generators may rely on it.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"pyxamstore\", \"concept\": \"Xamarin assemblies.blob / XALZ (row 55)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python pyxamstore` (or github jakev/pyxamstore). Then `pyxamstore unpack -d assemblies/` and ilspycmd. Also small prebuild: XALZ header (magic, index, size) + lz4.block decompress (lz4 in venv).\"},\n  {\"id\": \"apkid\", \"concept\": \"packer / obfuscator / anti-VM identification (rows 44-48)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip: `uv pip install --python .venv/bin/python apkid` (needs yara-python, already OK). `apkid -j x.apk` names packers, obfuscators and anti-debug in one call: a fast routing cue for an unseen theme.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"bundletool\", \"concept\": \"AAB / APKS packaging (row 58)\", \"priority\": 2, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release jar google/bundletool (bundletool-all-1.17.x.jar) into tools/bundletool + bin shim. `bundletool dump manifest --bundle x.aab`, `bundletool build-apks --mode=universal`. AAB manifests are protobuf, so aapt dump xmltree fails on them.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"generalize-before-stop\", \"concept\": \"carry the hand-solved method into solve.py when a live worker reaches CORRECT first\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"D23: hand-solved TT/Mastery left solve.py without a v2 path; the overnight prebuild fixed it and D24 went 3/3 on the solver alone. Keep the rule: when a timed mode is CORRECT via a live worker, let one generalize worker finish offline and require `hctf solver-test` on the variant-* cases with expected.json filled from confirmed.json.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"ios-ipa-readiness\", \"concept\": \"iOS IPA (row 64)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"note\", \"detail\": \"Lane is named mobile-android; if an .ipa ever ships: unzip Payload/, plistlib for Info.plist and binary plists, rz-bin -zz / lief for Mach-O strings, ipsw (github blacktop/ipsw release) for class-dump. Nothing to prebuild now.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"il2cppdumper\", \"concept\": \"Unity IL2CPP (row 56)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release Perfare/Il2CppDumper (or SamboyCoding/Cpp2IL) into tools/; run with bin/dotnet. Only if a Unity fixture ever ships.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"blutter\", \"concept\": \"Flutter Dart AOT (row 52)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github worawit/blutter (python3 blutter.py <lib dir> <out>; builds per Dart version with cmake/ninja + fetches the Dart SDK, slow first run; arm64 only). Alt: pip reflutter (needs repack + device: low value). Plain strings on libapp.so cover literal answers.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"abe\", \"concept\": \"encrypted Android backup (row 16)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"github release nelenkov/android-backup-extractor (abe.jar): `java -jar abe.jar unpack b.ab b.tar [pw]`. Needed only for encrypted .ab (PBKDF2+AES); unencrypted is zlib-flate.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"frida-tools\", \"concept\": \"dynamic instrumentation / root and frida checks (rows 47, 48)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"pip frida-tools / objection. Low value: no Android device or emulator here (adb present, no target), and every answer so far was static. Keep the rule: read the gated branch statically.\"},\n  {\"id\": \"standalone-baksmali\", \"concept\": \"smali-level reading / patching (row 51)\", \"priority\": 3, \"action\": \"tool\", \"detail\": \"Link tools/dex2jar/d2j-baksmali.sh + d2j-smali.sh into bin/ (already on disk), or github google/smali release. apktool d already emits smali, so cosmetic.\"}\n]\n```\n","numLines":99,"startLine":212,"totalLines":310}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_011VRGk737TWwSVczCrJjoSU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
