{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgQuSRBUjnfN8HYxwm1Ha","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UTKDrFHRKpvQ7CREnjn1dy","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/gaps26.py <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nblk=re.search(r'```json(.*?)```',s,re.S)\ngaps={g['id']:g for g in json.loads(blk.group(1))}\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"v2-split-asset-read\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain reads an asset from another APK of the install: ApplicationInfo.splitSourceDirs/sourceDir + java.util.zip.ZipFile, AssetManager.open across splits (rows 58, 102)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 TT and Mastery set10 went SILENT: `Assets.readSplit(\\\"huntress_feature.bin\\\")` = for p in ctx.getApplicationInfo().splitSourceDirs: z=new ZipFile(p); e=z.getEntry(\\\"assets/\\\"+name); if e!=null read up to 16 B via z.getInputStream(e).read(buf, off, len) loop, close, return; else throw FileNotFoundException; then `Util.mergeFeature*` folds b[0:8], b[8:16] as big-endian u64. The generalize worker's split-aware eval did not persist. Build it in lib (not solve.py): (1) bundle detection in puzzle_candidates/extract_answer -- outer zip whose members are PK APKs (.apks/.xapk/.apkm, `delivery N: *.apks`); base = member with huntress_puzzle.json (fallback: manifest without `split=`); (2) deep-evaluator intrinsics backed by the bundle: Context.getApplicationInfo() -> ApplicationInfo{sourceDir='/base.apk', splitSourceDirs=[...members except base, in bundle order], splitNames from each member's manifest `split=`, publicSourceDir, nativeLibraryDir, flags from the base manifest}, Context.getPackageCodePath, ZipFile(String|File).getEntry/getInputStream/entries/size/close, ZipEntry.getSize/getName/getCrc, InputStream.read()/read(byte[])/read(byte[],int,int)/readAllBytes/available/skip/close, DataInputStream.readLong/readInt/readFully, ByteBuffer.wrap(..).order(..).getLong/getInt, FileNotFoundException/IOException as modelled exceptions, AssetManager.open(name) searching base then splits, Context.createContextForSplit(name).getAssets(). (3) Regression: the D26 TT and set10 cases (expected from confirmed.json) + a synthetic variant with 2 feature splits where only one holds the named entry. Keep <0.4 s/set.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-config-device-select\",\"concept\":\"several configuration splits (ABI / density / locale); only the one the pinned device would install counts (rows 58, 104)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 prompt says 'base and configuration splits' but shipped only a feature split -- the TT/Mastery mutation or a later day may ship split_config.x86_64.apk + split_config.arm64_v8a.apk (+ xxhdpi/xhdpi, en/fr) each carrying an evidence asset/fragment, with the non-matching ones as decoys. Parse each member's binary manifest (`split=\\\"config.x86_64\\\"`, `configForSplit`, `isFeatureSplit`, `<uses-split>`, `requiredSplitTypes`/`splitTypes`) and toc.pb / XAPK manifest.json `split_apks` if present. Device profile = the solve oracle's pinned emulator: ABI x86_64 (fallback x86, then arm64-v8a only if no x86 split), density 420/440 dpi -> xxhdpi bucket, locale en-US; feature splits always installed. Expose `bundle_install_set(data) -> [members]` used by v2-split-asset-read's splitSourceDirs and by v1 fragment filling; when fragments from several config splits compete for one `part_index`, take the installed one and log the others. Report both the selected and the all-splits value if they differ.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-feature-dex-code\",\"concept\":\"code shipped in a feature split (split classes.dex; isolatedSplits split ClassLoader; SplitCompat / SplitInstallManager) called from the base chain (rows 42, 101, 103)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 feature split had hasCode=false; the obvious next step is hasCode=true with its own classes.dex holding one link of the token chain. Base calls it as a normal static invoke (non-isolated splits share the base PathClassLoader: merge class tables, base wins on duplicate descriptors) or via `ctx.createContextForSplit(\\\"arena_feature\\\").getClassLoader().loadClass(name)` / `Class.forName(name, true, loader)` + getDeclaredMethod.invoke (isolatedSplits=true in the base manifest: split loader's parent = base loader). Play Core: `SplitCompat.install(ctx)` -> true, `SplitInstallManagerFactory.create(ctx).getInstalledModules()` -> set of feature split names in the bundle. Extend the deep evaluator to load every installed member's classes*.dex into the right loader and continue evaluation inside them; reuse classloader-shadow-resolve. Fixture: synthetic bundle built from a D26 base + a small split dex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-native-lib-config-abi\",\"concept\":\"libarena.so shipped in an ABI config split (split_config.x86_64.apk) and reached via System.loadLibrary from the base chain (rows 37, 58, 104)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Bundletool puts native libs in ABI config splits, never in base.apk. If a D15/D16-style native hop (`nativeShare(long[,int])`) moves into a split bundle, solve.py's `_native_call` looks only inside the APK it was given and fails. Make the unicorn JNI hop resolve `System.loadLibrary(\\\"arena\\\")` across the install set from split-config-device-select (x86_64 first; arm64-v8a only with an aarch64 unicorn mode if no x86_64 split), honour `android:extractNativeLibs`, and cache the Uc per .so sha256. Also handle libs under `lib/<abi>/` of a FEATURE split. Regression: repackage the D25 d16 Mastery set as base + split_config.x86_64.apk.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bundle-container-formats\",\"concept\":\"other multi-APK containers: XAPK (manifest.json + OBB), APKM (info.json), bundletool .apks with toc.pb, AAB (protobuf manifests, base/ + feature/ modules), zip-in-zip (rows 58, 62)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 used a bare stored zip of 2 APKs. Variants of the same theme: `.xapk` (`manifest.json` with `split_apks:[{file,id}]`, `package_name`, optional `Android/obb/<pkg>/main.N.<pkg>.obb` zip holding assets), `.apkm` (unencrypted `info.json` + `base.apk` + `split_config.*.apk`), bundletool `.apks` (`toc.pb` BuildApksResult: variants -> apk_set -> module_metadata/apk_description with split_apk_metadata.split_id and targeting) and `standalones/`, `.aab` (`base/manifest/AndroidManifest.xml` protobuf XmlNode, `base/dex/classes.dex`, `base/assets/`, `<feature>/...`, `BundleConfig.pb`). Normalize all of them into one `Bundle(members: name -> (manifest facts, zip bytes or dir view))` consumed by puzzle_candidates, v2-split-asset-read and split-config-device-select; reuse aab-proto-manifest-parse and nested-container-recurse; protobuf via the lib wire decoder (no protoc). Pure python, <50 ms per bundle.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-resources-arsc-overlay\",\"concept\":\"chain reads Resources (getString/getIdentifier/getInteger/openRawResource) whose value lives in a split's resources.arsc or overrides base per config (rows 22, 61, 104)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Feature splits carry their own resources.arsc (package id 0x7f shared or 0x80+ for isolated), config splits carry density/locale-qualified overrides of base entries. Parse every member's arsc (ResTable_package, type specs, ResTable_config: density, locale, sdk), build the merged table the pinned device would see (x86_64 emulator, 420 dpi -> xxhdpi, en-US) and serve `ctx.getResources().getString(id)`, `getIdentifier(name, type, pkg)`, `getInteger`, `getStringArray`, `openRawResource(id)` / `res/raw/*` from the right split. Reuse resource-id-const-resolve. Fallback scan: report every distinct value per config so a worker sees the override.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-signature-digest-binding\",\"concept\":\"base verifies that a split belongs to it before folding its bytes: same signer cert, split versionCode/revisionCode, MANIFEST.MF/SHA-256 digest pinned in base (rows 49, 59, 83, 104)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 STRUCTURAL 'base and feature split correlation' -- the next turn of the screw is a correlation CHECK: two candidate feature splits (or a split per config) where only one has the base's signing cert (v1 FIXTURE-.RSA / v2 block cert SHA-256), the base's `versionCode` + matching `android:revisionCode`, or an asset whose SHA-256/CRC32 (ZipEntry.getCrc) equals a `const-wide`/hex string in the base dex. Provide: per-member signer cert digest (v1 PKCS#7 + v2/v3 block, pure python), manifest versionCode/revisionCode/split name, entry CRC32/SHA-256, MessageDigest/CRC32 intrinsics over ZipFile entry bytes in the deep evaluator, and PackageManager.getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signingInfo.getApkContentsSigners()[0].toByteArray() returning the base cert DER. Select the member that passes; log the decoys.\"},\n {\"id\":\"janus-dex-apk-polyglot\",\"concept\":\"APK that is also a dex (Janus, CVE-2017-13156): dex bytes prepended before the zip, v1-only signature; the 'decision' is which view the runtime loads (rows 62, 105)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Packaging-arc follow-up to D26. Detect `dex\\\\n03x` magic at offset 0 of an .apk whose EOCD still parses (zip central directory offsets shifted by the dex size, or a dex `file_size` < file length with the zip appended). On Android < 8 with a v1-only signature the runtime executes the PREPENDED dex, not classes.dex: evaluate both, label them ('runtime view' vs 'zip view'), prefer the runtime view when minSdk < 26 and no v2 block. Also catch the reverse polyglot (dex appended after EOCD / in the zip comment) and an APK Signing Block carrying an extra payload ID. Pure python over the raw bytes; reuse zip-structure-anomaly-scan for the zip side.\"},\n {\"id\":\"apk-signing-v3-rotation-lineage\",\"concept\":\"APK Signature Scheme v3/v3.1 key rotation (proof-of-rotation lineage of past -> current signers) and v4 .idsig (rows 59, 105)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If the packaging arc continues ('which signer is the app?'), the answer or a chain input may depend on the CURRENT signer vs the original one. Parse the APK Signing Block: v2 0x7109871a, v3 0xf05368c0, v3.1 0x1b93ad61 (min/max SDK targeting), proof-of-rotation attribute 0x3ba06f8c (lineage nodes: signed data, cert, flags, sig alg), stripping protection 0xbeeff00d; v4 `.idsig` (version, hashing info, merkle root, signing info). Output per scheme: signer cert DER SHA-256 / SHA-1 / subject, lineage order and capability flags, which signer a device at the pinned emulator's SDK (34) would report via signingInfo.getApkContentsSigners() vs getSigningCertificateHistory(). Pure python; extend cert-and-signing-facts output.\"},\n]\norder=[\"v2-split-asset-read\",\"split-config-device-select\",\"split-feature-dex-code\",\"split-native-lib-config-abi\",\"worker-cue-inline\",\n       \"bundle-container-formats\",\"split-signature-digest-binding\",\"split-resources-arsc-overlay\",\"janus-dex-apk-polyglot\",\"apk-signing-v3-rotation-lineage\",\"v2-reflection-api-breadth\",\n       \"bundletool\",\"apkid\",\"pyxamstore\",\"generalize-before-stop\",\"ios-ipa-readiness\",\"il2cppdumper\",\"blutter\",\"abe\",\"frida-tools\",\"standalone-baksmali\"]\nfor g in new: gaps[g['id']]=g\ngaps['bundletool']['detail']=\"D26 shipped a bare .apks (no toc.pb); config-split / AAB variants are now plausible. \"+gaps['bundletool']['detail']\ngaps['worker-cue-inline']['detail']=\"D26: the cue for `*.apks` (list every member; the evidence lives in the OTHER split) is now in steps 0/1/5b. \"+gaps['worker-cue-inline']['detail']\ngaps['generalize-before-stop']['detail']=\"D26 repeat: the mastery generalize worker wrote a split-aware eval that never persisted in solve.py. \"+gaps['generalize-before-stop']['detail']\nassert set(order)==set(gaps), set(gaps)^set(order)\nout=[gaps[i] for i in order]\njs=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+\"\\n]\\n\"\njson.loads(js)\ns=s[:blk.start(1)]+js+s[blk.end(1):]\ni=s.index(\"Forecast after D25:\"); j=s.index(\"```json\")\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"Forecast after D26: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc (D21 anti-debug -> D25 Play Integrity) gave way to a PACKAGING turn: D26\n\"Split Decision\" shipped a real 2-APK `.apks` and the first v2 chain that READS ARTIFACT BYTES (feature-split asset via\n`splitSourceDirs` + `ZipFile`). The prompt named \"configuration splits\" that did not ship yet -> config-split selection,\ncode/native libs inside splits and split binding checks are the likeliest D27-D28 TT mutations or Mastery repeats\n(priority 1). The packaging thread can run on: signing schemes (v3 rotation, Janus polyglot), AAB/XAPK containers, split\nresources. Still unnamed for D27-D31 (5 days): certificate pinning, key attestation, tamper/repackaging, the obfuscation\ncapstones (flattening, VM, white-box) and probably an all-days capstone. Mastery: 10 sets on D26 (+1/day -> ~15 by D31);\nold days due as v2: d05, d08, d12, d18, d20 (d11/d13/d21 came PURE on D26). Mastery solve 1.13 s for 9 sets.\n\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/gaps26.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\ns=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read()\ng=json.loads(re.search(r'```json(.*?)```',s,re.S).group(1))\nst=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not ((st.get('mobile-android:'+x['id']) or {}).get('ok') or (st.get('mobile-android:'+x['id']) or {}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g),'gaps;',len(pend),'pending prebuild:',pend); print(all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g))\nEOF\nwc -l reference/coverage/mobile-android.md; rm -f $TMPDIR/gaps26.py"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":547,"cache_read_input_tokens":135785,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":547},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0b5a4874-41a3-4f1d-b581-92bd56f6f405","uuid":"f722b932-26f1-48f1-86e1-e97ba9d0b68c","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:11:54.425Z","request_id":"req_011CgQuSQnQwv3RkS1DD4Voh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01UTKDrFHRKpvQ7CREnjn1dy":{"command":"cd /home/testpwn/huntress-2026; cat > $TMPDIR/gaps26.py <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\np='reference/coverage/mobile-android.md'\ns=open(p).read()\nblk=re.search(r'```json(.*?)```',s,re.S)\ngaps={g['id']:g for g in json.loads(blk.group(1))}\nnew=[\n {\"id\":\"v2-split-asset-read\",\"concept\":\"v2 chain reads an asset from another APK of the install: ApplicationInfo.splitSourceDirs/sourceDir + java.util.zip.ZipFile, AssetManager.open across splits (rows 58, 102)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 TT and Mastery set10 went SILENT: `Assets.readSplit(\\\"huntress_feature.bin\\\")` = for p in ctx.getApplicationInfo().splitSourceDirs: z=new ZipFile(p); e=z.getEntry(\\\"assets/\\\"+name); if e!=null read up to 16 B via z.getInputStream(e).read(buf, off, len) loop, close, return; else throw FileNotFoundException; then `Util.mergeFeature*` folds b[0:8], b[8:16] as big-endian u64. The generalize worker's split-aware eval did not persist. Build it in lib (not solve.py): (1) bundle detection in puzzle_candidates/extract_answer -- outer zip whose members are PK APKs (.apks/.xapk/.apkm, `delivery N: *.apks`); base = member with huntress_puzzle.json (fallback: manifest without `split=`); (2) deep-evaluator intrinsics backed by the bundle: Context.getApplicationInfo() -> ApplicationInfo{sourceDir='/base.apk', splitSourceDirs=[...members except base, in bundle order], splitNames from each member's manifest `split=`, publicSourceDir, nativeLibraryDir, flags from the base manifest}, Context.getPackageCodePath, ZipFile(String|File).getEntry/getInputStream/entries/size/close, ZipEntry.getSize/getName/getCrc, InputStream.read()/read(byte[])/read(byte[],int,int)/readAllBytes/available/skip/close, DataInputStream.readLong/readInt/readFully, ByteBuffer.wrap(..).order(..).getLong/getInt, FileNotFoundException/IOException as modelled exceptions, AssetManager.open(name) searching base then splits, Context.createContextForSplit(name).getAssets(). (3) Regression: the D26 TT and set10 cases (expected from confirmed.json) + a synthetic variant with 2 feature splits where only one holds the named entry. Keep <0.4 s/set.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-config-device-select\",\"concept\":\"several configuration splits (ABI / density / locale); only the one the pinned device would install counts (rows 58, 104)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 prompt says 'base and configuration splits' but shipped only a feature split -- the TT/Mastery mutation or a later day may ship split_config.x86_64.apk + split_config.arm64_v8a.apk (+ xxhdpi/xhdpi, en/fr) each carrying an evidence asset/fragment, with the non-matching ones as decoys. Parse each member's binary manifest (`split=\\\"config.x86_64\\\"`, `configForSplit`, `isFeatureSplit`, `<uses-split>`, `requiredSplitTypes`/`splitTypes`) and toc.pb / XAPK manifest.json `split_apks` if present. Device profile = the solve oracle's pinned emulator: ABI x86_64 (fallback x86, then arm64-v8a only if no x86 split), density 420/440 dpi -> xxhdpi bucket, locale en-US; feature splits always installed. Expose `bundle_install_set(data) -> [members]` used by v2-split-asset-read's splitSourceDirs and by v1 fragment filling; when fragments from several config splits compete for one `part_index`, take the installed one and log the others. Report both the selected and the all-splits value if they differ.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-feature-dex-code\",\"concept\":\"code shipped in a feature split (split classes.dex; isolatedSplits split ClassLoader; SplitCompat / SplitInstallManager) called from the base chain (rows 42, 101, 103)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 feature split had hasCode=false; the obvious next step is hasCode=true with its own classes.dex holding one link of the token chain. Base calls it as a normal static invoke (non-isolated splits share the base PathClassLoader: merge class tables, base wins on duplicate descriptors) or via `ctx.createContextForSplit(\\\"arena_feature\\\").getClassLoader().loadClass(name)` / `Class.forName(name, true, loader)` + getDeclaredMethod.invoke (isolatedSplits=true in the base manifest: split loader's parent = base loader). Play Core: `SplitCompat.install(ctx)` -> true, `SplitInstallManagerFactory.create(ctx).getInstalledModules()` -> set of feature split names in the bundle. Extend the deep evaluator to load every installed member's classes*.dex into the right loader and continue evaluation inside them; reuse classloader-shadow-resolve. Fixture: synthetic bundle built from a D26 base + a small split dex.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-native-lib-config-abi\",\"concept\":\"libarena.so shipped in an ABI config split (split_config.x86_64.apk) and reached via System.loadLibrary from the base chain (rows 37, 58, 104)\",\"priority\":1,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Bundletool puts native libs in ABI config splits, never in base.apk. If a D15/D16-style native hop (`nativeShare(long[,int])`) moves into a split bundle, solve.py's `_native_call` looks only inside the APK it was given and fails. Make the unicorn JNI hop resolve `System.loadLibrary(\\\"arena\\\")` across the install set from split-config-device-select (x86_64 first; arm64-v8a only with an aarch64 unicorn mode if no x86_64 split), honour `android:extractNativeLibs`, and cache the Uc per .so sha256. Also handle libs under `lib/<abi>/` of a FEATURE split. Regression: repackage the D25 d16 Mastery set as base + split_config.x86_64.apk.\"},\n {\"id\":\"bundle-container-formats\",\"concept\":\"other multi-APK containers: XAPK (manifest.json + OBB), APKM (info.json), bundletool .apks with toc.pb, AAB (protobuf manifests, base/ + feature/ modules), zip-in-zip (rows 58, 62)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 used a bare stored zip of 2 APKs. Variants of the same theme: `.xapk` (`manifest.json` with `split_apks:[{file,id}]`, `package_name`, optional `Android/obb/<pkg>/main.N.<pkg>.obb` zip holding assets), `.apkm` (unencrypted `info.json` + `base.apk` + `split_config.*.apk`), bundletool `.apks` (`toc.pb` BuildApksResult: variants -> apk_set -> module_metadata/apk_description with split_apk_metadata.split_id and targeting) and `standalones/`, `.aab` (`base/manifest/AndroidManifest.xml` protobuf XmlNode, `base/dex/classes.dex`, `base/assets/`, `<feature>/...`, `BundleConfig.pb`). Normalize all of them into one `Bundle(members: name -> (manifest facts, zip bytes or dir view))` consumed by puzzle_candidates, v2-split-asset-read and split-config-device-select; reuse aab-proto-manifest-parse and nested-container-recurse; protobuf via the lib wire decoder (no protoc). Pure python, <50 ms per bundle.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-resources-arsc-overlay\",\"concept\":\"chain reads Resources (getString/getIdentifier/getInteger/openRawResource) whose value lives in a split's resources.arsc or overrides base per config (rows 22, 61, 104)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Feature splits carry their own resources.arsc (package id 0x7f shared or 0x80+ for isolated), config splits carry density/locale-qualified overrides of base entries. Parse every member's arsc (ResTable_package, type specs, ResTable_config: density, locale, sdk), build the merged table the pinned device would see (x86_64 emulator, 420 dpi -> xxhdpi, en-US) and serve `ctx.getResources().getString(id)`, `getIdentifier(name, type, pkg)`, `getInteger`, `getStringArray`, `openRawResource(id)` / `res/raw/*` from the right split. Reuse resource-id-const-resolve. Fallback scan: report every distinct value per config so a worker sees the override.\"},\n {\"id\":\"split-signature-digest-binding\",\"concept\":\"base verifies that a split belongs to it before folding its bytes: same signer cert, split versionCode/revisionCode, MANIFEST.MF/SHA-256 digest pinned in base (rows 49, 59, 83, 104)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"D26 STRUCTURAL 'base and feature split correlation' -- the next turn of the screw is a correlation CHECK: two candidate feature splits (or a split per config) where only one has the base's signing cert (v1 FIXTURE-.RSA / v2 block cert SHA-256), the base's `versionCode` + matching `android:revisionCode`, or an asset whose SHA-256/CRC32 (ZipEntry.getCrc) equals a `const-wide`/hex string in the base dex. Provide: per-member signer cert digest (v1 PKCS#7 + v2/v3 block, pure python), manifest versionCode/revisionCode/split name, entry CRC32/SHA-256, MessageDigest/CRC32 intrinsics over ZipFile entry bytes in the deep evaluator, and PackageManager.getPackageInfo(pkg, GET_SIGNING_CERTIFICATES).signingInfo.getApkContentsSigners()[0].toByteArray() returning the base cert DER. Select the member that passes; log the decoys.\"},\n {\"id\":\"janus-dex-apk-polyglot\",\"concept\":\"APK that is also a dex (Janus, CVE-2017-13156): dex bytes prepended before the zip, v1-only signature; the 'decision' is which view the runtime loads (rows 62, 105)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"Packaging-arc follow-up to D26. Detect `dex\\\\n03x` magic at offset 0 of an .apk whose EOCD still parses (zip central directory offsets shifted by the dex size, or a dex `file_size` < file length with the zip appended). On Android < 8 with a v1-only signature the runtime executes the PREPENDED dex, not classes.dex: evaluate both, label them ('runtime view' vs 'zip view'), prefer the runtime view when minSdk < 26 and no v2 block. Also catch the reverse polyglot (dex appended after EOCD / in the zip comment) and an APK Signing Block carrying an extra payload ID. Pure python over the raw bytes; reuse zip-structure-anomaly-scan for the zip side.\"},\n {\"id\":\"apk-signing-v3-rotation-lineage\",\"concept\":\"APK Signature Scheme v3/v3.1 key rotation (proof-of-rotation lineage of past -> current signers) and v4 .idsig (rows 59, 105)\",\"priority\":2,\"action\":\"prebuild\",\"detail\":\"If the packaging arc continues ('which signer is the app?'), the answer or a chain input may depend on the CURRENT signer vs the original one. Parse the APK Signing Block: v2 0x7109871a, v3 0xf05368c0, v3.1 0x1b93ad61 (min/max SDK targeting), proof-of-rotation attribute 0x3ba06f8c (lineage nodes: signed data, cert, flags, sig alg), stripping protection 0xbeeff00d; v4 `.idsig` (version, hashing info, merkle root, signing info). Output per scheme: signer cert DER SHA-256 / SHA-1 / subject, lineage order and capability flags, which signer a device at the pinned emulator's SDK (34) would report via signingInfo.getApkContentsSigners() vs getSigningCertificateHistory(). Pure python; extend cert-and-signing-facts output.\"},\n]\norder=[\"v2-split-asset-read\",\"split-config-device-select\",\"split-feature-dex-code\",\"split-native-lib-config-abi\",\"worker-cue-inline\",\n       \"bundle-container-formats\",\"split-signature-digest-binding\",\"split-resources-arsc-overlay\",\"janus-dex-apk-polyglot\",\"apk-signing-v3-rotation-lineage\",\"v2-reflection-api-breadth\",\n       \"bundletool\",\"apkid\",\"pyxamstore\",\"generalize-before-stop\",\"ios-ipa-readiness\",\"il2cppdumper\",\"blutter\",\"abe\",\"frida-tools\",\"standalone-baksmali\"]\nfor g in new: gaps[g['id']]=g\ngaps['bundletool']['detail']=\"D26 shipped a bare .apks (no toc.pb); config-split / AAB variants are now plausible. \"+gaps['bundletool']['detail']\ngaps['worker-cue-inline']['detail']=\"D26: the cue for `*.apks` (list every member; the evidence lives in the OTHER split) is now in steps 0/1/5b. \"+gaps['worker-cue-inline']['detail']\ngaps['generalize-before-stop']['detail']=\"D26 repeat: the mastery generalize worker wrote a split-aware eval that never persisted in solve.py. \"+gaps['generalize-before-stop']['detail']\nassert set(order)==set(gaps), set(gaps)^set(order)\nout=[gaps[i] for i in order]\njs=\"[\\n\"+\",\\n\".join(\"  \"+json.dumps(g,ensure_ascii=False) for g in out)+\"\\n]\\n\"\njson.loads(js)\ns=s[:blk.start(1)]+js+s[blk.end(1):]\ni=s.index(\"Forecast after D25:\"); j=s.index(\"```json\")\ns=s[:i]+\"\"\"Forecast after D26: the MASVS-RESILIENCE arc (D21 anti-debug -> D25 Play Integrity) gave way to a PACKAGING turn: D26\n\"Split Decision\" shipped a real 2-APK `.apks` and the first v2 chain that READS ARTIFACT BYTES (feature-split asset via\n`splitSourceDirs` + `ZipFile`). The prompt named \"configuration splits\" that did not ship yet -> config-split selection,\ncode/native libs inside splits and split binding checks are the likeliest D27-D28 TT mutations or Mastery repeats\n(priority 1). The packaging thread can run on: signing schemes (v3 rotation, Janus polyglot), AAB/XAPK containers, split\nresources. Still unnamed for D27-D31 (5 days): certificate pinning, key attestation, tamper/repackaging, the obfuscation\ncapstones (flattening, VM, white-box) and probably an all-days capstone. Mastery: 10 sets on D26 (+1/day -> ~15 by D31);\nold days due as v2: d05, d08, d12, d18, d20 (d11/d13/d21 came PURE on D26). Mastery solve 1.13 s for 9 sets.\n\n\"\"\"+s[j:]\nopen(p,'w').write(s)\nEOF\npython3 $TMPDIR/gaps26.py && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport json,re\ns=open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/reference/coverage/mobile-android.md').read()\ng=json.loads(re.search(r'```json(.*?)```',s,re.S).group(1))\nst=json.load(open('/home/testpwn/huntress-2026/.run/prebuild-state.json'))\npend=[x['id'] for x in g if x['action']=='prebuild' and not ((st.get('mobile-android:'+x['id']) or {}).get('ok') or (st.get('mobile-android:'+x['id']) or {}).get('attempts',0)>=2)]\nprint(len(g),'gaps;',len(pend),'pending prebuild:',pend); print(all(set(x)=={'id','concept','priority','action','detail'} for x in g))\nEOF\nwc -l reference/coverage/mobile-android.md; rm -f $TMPDIR/gaps26.py"}}}
